---
// The same buggy close() (save first, set status after) checked two ways.
// Values are the -v --runxfail capture: mock PASSED, fake FAILED with 'open' == 'closed'.
const W = 900, H = 330;
---
<figure class="bep9c">
  <div class="bep9c-scroll">
  <svg viewBox={`0 0 ${W} ${H}`} role="img" aria-label="Two columns checking the same buggy close method. Left, a mock repository: the test asks whether save was called once and it passes. Right, a fake repository that stores a copy: the test reads the stored status, finds open instead of closed, and fails.">
    <text x="215" y="28" text-anchor="middle" class="h">
      <tspan data-lang-en>with a mock</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>với mock</tspan>
    </text>
    <text x="685" y="28" text-anchor="middle" class="h">
      <tspan data-lang-en>with a fake</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>với fake</tspan>
    </text>

    <rect x="40" y="50" width="350" height="64" rx="10" class="box" />
    <text x="60" y="78" class="code">repo.save(case)</text>
    <text x="60" y="100" class="bs"><tspan data-lang-en>called once, as the test expects</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>được gọi một lần, đúng như test mong</tspan></text>
    <line x1="215" y1="114" x2="215" y2="150" class="ln" />
    <polygon points="215,160 210,150 220,150" class="hd" />
    <rect x="40" y="160" width="350" height="64" rx="10" class="box" />
    <text x="60" y="188" class="code">assert_called_once()</text>
    <text x="60" y="210" class="bs"><tspan data-lang-en>asks what the code did, not what it stored</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>hỏi code đã làm gì, không hỏi đã lưu gì</tspan></text>
    <line x1="215" y1="224" x2="215" y2="258" class="ln" />
    <polygon points="215,268 210,258 220,258" class="hd" />
    <text x="215" y="296" text-anchor="middle" class="verdict redt">
      <tspan data-lang-en>PASSED, and the bug ships</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>PASSED, và bug được ship</tspan>
    </text>

    <rect x="510" y="50" width="350" height="64" rx="10" class="box" />
    <text x="530" y="78" class="code">fake.save(copy of case)</text>
    <text x="530" y="100" class="bs"><tspan data-lang-en>copied while status was still "open"</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>copy lúc status vẫn là "open"</tspan></text>
    <line x1="685" y1="114" x2="685" y2="150" class="ln" />
    <polygon points="685,160 680,150 690,150" class="hd" />
    <rect x="510" y="160" width="350" height="64" rx="10" class="box" />
    <text x="530" y="188" class="code">fake.get("C-1").status</text>
    <text x="530" y="210" class="bs"><tspan data-lang-en>reads what storage holds: "open"</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>đọc thứ kho thật đang giữ: "open"</tspan></text>
    <line x1="685" y1="224" x2="685" y2="258" class="ln" />
    <polygon points="685,268 680,258 690,258" class="hd" />
    <text x="685" y="296" text-anchor="middle" class="verdict">
      <tspan data-lang-en>FAILED: 'open' == 'closed'</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>FAILED: 'open' == 'closed'</tspan>
    </text>
  </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    <span data-lang-en>The mock only knows what you told it to expect, so it agrees with whatever the code does. The fake keeps state the way storage does, so it can disagree.</span>
    <span data-lang-vi>Mock chỉ biết điều bạn bảo nó mong đợi, nên code làm gì nó cũng gật đầu. Fake giữ trạng thái giống kho thật, nên nó có thể phản đối.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .bep9c { margin: 2em 0; width: 100%; }
  .bep9c-scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  .bep9c svg { display: block; width: 100%; min-width: 700px; height: auto; }
  .bep9c text { font-size: 14px; fill: var(--text-body); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .bep9c .h { font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); font-size: 15px; }
  .bep9c .code { font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', ui-monospace, monospace; font-size: 13px; fill: var(--text); }
  .bep9c .bs { fill: var(--text-muted); font-size: 12.5px; }
  .bep9c .verdict { font-weight: 700; font-size: 16px; fill: var(--text); }
  .bep9c .redt { fill: var(--red); }
  .bep9c .box { fill: var(--bg-alt); stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1.4; }
  .bep9c .ln { stroke: var(--text-muted); stroke-width: 1.6; }
  .bep9c .hd { fill: var(--text-muted); }
  .bep9c figcaption { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.55; text-align: center; }
</style>
